Human-Operated Ransomware Attempt via Exposed RDP (MST-1198)

Severity: Critical
Status: Confirmed Multi-Stage Intrusion – Ransomware Prevented
Environment: Windows Domain (Active Directory)

1. Executive Summary

Between January 18–23, 2026, a human-operated ransomware intrusion was conducted against the MTS environment following unauthorized external RDP access to the domain controller. The attacker leveraged compromised administrator credentials to gain entry, perform reconnaissance, harvest additional credentials, and move laterally across the network.

A staged malware chain (ClipBanker → Installer → Amadey → Ransomware payload) was deployed on downstream hosts. Microsoft Defender disrupted the attack prior to encryption, preventing business impact.

