4. Attack Overview
Initial Access

The attacker gained entry through externally exposed RDP (no MFA) using compromised administrator credentials.

Lateral Movement

After accessing the domain controller, the attacker pivoted internally using RDP:

External → Domain Controller

Domain Controller → mts-contractorpc1

Domain Controller → mts-pc-1 (using stolen zach.balrog credentials)

Malware Deployment

On mts-pc-1, the attacker executed:

ClipBanker (initial loader)

Secondary installer

Amadey botnet loader (masquerading as system process)

Setup[1].exe (ransomware staging payload)

Amadey performed process injection, established persistence, and downloaded additional payloads.

5. Technical Findings

RDP exposed externally without MFA

Administrator credentials reused after compromise

Credential harvesting enabled secondary account abuse

Registry-based persistence established

Process injection observed

Ransomware components staged but not executed

Defender successfully blocked encryption phase

This intrusion demonstrates hands-on-keyboard activity consistent with human-operated ransomware campaigns.

